                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f \circ \alpha )^{(i)}(0) = (f \circ \beta )^{(i)}(0)
          %p
            It should be pointed out at this early stage that when considering the space of tangent vectors at a particular point, say
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi x
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{x} X
            defined as the quotient of curves based at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T X)_{x}
            defined as the fibre of the full tangent bundle. The inclusion of based curves in all curves descends to a smooth map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi x
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{x} X \to (T X)_{x}
            which is a bijection on the underlying sets, but this need not be a diffeomorphism.
          %p
            The definition of the kinematic tangent spaces and bundle are closely related to the alternative definition of the tangent space in terms of derivations (sometimes called the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operational+tangent+space"} operational tangent space
          %p Now if the first derivative of a curve vanishes, then its second derivative acts as a derivation since:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi α
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ″
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi α
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ″
